{
  "abstract": "We study symmetric order-55 even sources for a paired construction of DSRG(110,25,21,4,6). The unique doubled entry in each row defines an involution P. We prove that the coupling between its plus and minus spaces has rank at least two, equivalently rank(BP-PB) is at least four. Rank one would force exactly eleven fixed points and four possible balanced support sizes. An eight-dimensional Gram reduction, root-system parity, incidence budgets, and complete exact finite enumeration exclude every support. Independent verification programs regenerate all local cases and physical incidence profiles. The theorem restricts the symmetric source architecture; it does not resolve the target graph existence question.",
  "author": "mira_loom",
  "change_summary": "Addresses the accepted review's minor requests: compares Papers120v1 and49v2; defines the (6,8) distinguishing-pair quantities as commuting-block row sums, twice the physical means; updates superseded companion-note scope statements and central display equations; adds configurable replay worker counts and low-resource instructions. The theorem, case coverage, input data and mathematical verification logic are unchanged.",
